README.md:495:- [`LivingEntity`](Engine.Models/LivingEntity.cs) is the abstract base for anything with HP, gold, a level, attributes and an inventory. It exposes `TakeDamage`, `Heal`, `CompleteHeal`, `ReceiveGold`, `SpendGold`, `AddItemToInventory`, `RemoveItemFromInventory`, `UseCurrentWeaponOn(target)` and `UseCurrentConsumable()`. It raises `OnKilled` and relays its equipped item's action text as `OnActionPerformed`.
README.md:502:- [`Battle`](Engine.Models/Battle.cs) owns one fight. The constructor only subscribes to both combatants' events. `Start()` announces the monster and rolls initiative, so the monster may strike first. That happens outside the constructor so that `GameSession` already holds the battle if the first strike kills the player. The battle then runs the attack → counter-attack exchange, hands out rewards and raises `OnCombatVictory`. It is `IDisposable` so it can unhook its event handlers.
README.md:529:| **Weaved `INotifyPropertyChanged`** | `FodyWeavers.xml` in Models and ViewModels (`<PropertyChanged />`) | Classes only declare `event PropertyChanged`. Fody injects the notify calls into every setter at compile time, including for computed properties that depend on them (`IsAlive`, `HasMonster`, `HasLocationToNorth`…). `[DoNotCheckEquality]` on `CurrentLocation` makes the setter run even when you "move" to the same location, for example respawning at Home while already there. |
README.md:530:| **Factory + Prototype** | `ItemFactory`, `MonsterFactory`, … | Data is parsed once. Each request gets a `Clone()`, so two Snakes (or two Pointy sticks) never share HP, weapons or event subscribers. |
README.md:532:| **Observer / events** | See the event table below | Loose coupling between actions, entities, battles, the session and the UI. |
